REGENT OF REJANG LEBONG

BENGKULU PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF REJANG LEBONG REGENCY

NUMBER 4 OF 2015

CONCERNING

PREVENTION AND MANAGEMENT OF VIOLENCE

AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF REJANG LEBONG,

Considering:
a. that in order to guarantee the rights of women and children so that they can participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and worth, and receive protection from violence, discrimination and other violations of the rights of women and children, it is necessary to undertake efforts to prevent and manage violence against women and children.
b. that in order for the efforts to prevent and manage violence against women and children to obtain optimal results, and be implemented quickly, in a planned, integrated, comprehensive and organized manner by involving all relevant elements in the region, it is necessary to have regulations concerning the prevention and management of violence against women and child victims of violence.
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Prevention and Management of Violence Against Women and Children.

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 28 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 4 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 55), Emergency Law Number 5 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 56) and Emergency Law Number 6 of 1956 (State Gazette of 1956 Number 57) concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions Including Municipalities, Within the Level I Region of South Sumatra, as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1821);
